## Third-Party Open Source Attributions

SlothWatch relies upon and attributes the following open-source libraries:

- **@browserbasehq/stagehand** (MIT License)
  Copyright (c) Browserbase, Inc.
  Cloud browser automation and AI-ready browser control.

- **better-sqlite3** (MIT License)
  Copyright (c) Joshua Wise
  Fast, embedded, synchronous SQLite3 library for Node.js.

- **commander** (MIT License)
  Copyright (c) TJ Holowaychuk
  The complete solution for Node.js command-line interfaces.

- **zod** (MIT License)
  Copyright (c) Colin McDonnell
  TypeScript-first schema declaration and validation with static type inference.

- **vitest** (MIT License)
  Copyright (c) Anthony Fu and Vitest contributors
  Next-generation testing framework powered by Vite.

- **picocolors** (ISC License)
  Copyright (c) Alexey Raspopov
  Lightweight library for formatting terminal output with ANSI colors.

- **tsx** (MIT License)
  Copyright (c) Privatenumber
  TypeScript Execute: Node.js enhanced with esbuild to run TypeScript files.
